sing rollback, and treating assumptions as dependencies.\n39: -->\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n44: ## 1. SUMMARY\n45: \n46: ### Technical Context\n47: \n48: | Aspect | Value |\n49: |--------|-------|\n50: | **Language/Stack** | [e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n51: | **Framework** | [e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n52: | **Storage** | [e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n53: | **Testing** | [e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n54: \n55: ### Overview\n56: [2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n57: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n62: ## 2. QUALITY GATES\n63: \n64: ### Definition of Ready\n65: - [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n66: - [ ] Success criteria measurable\n67: - [ ] Dependencies identified\n68: \n69: ### Definition of Done\n70: - [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n71: - [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n72: - [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: <!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n78: ## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n79: \n80: ### Pattern\n81: [MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n82: \n83: ### Key Components\n84: - **[Component 1]**: [Purpose]\n85: - **[Component 2]**: [Purpose]\n86: \n87: ### Data Flow\n88: [Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n89: <!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: <!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n94: ## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n95: \n96: Use this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n97: \n98: | Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n99: |---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n100: | [producer/helper/policy] | [what owns the behavior] | [update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [grep/test/doc evidence] |\n101: | [consumer/status/docs/tests] | [how it observes the behavior] | [update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [grep/test/doc evidence] |\n102: \n103: Required inventories:\n104: - Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n105: - Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n106: - Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n107: - Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n108: <!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: <!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n113: ## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n114: \n115: ### Phase 1: Setup\n116: - [ ] Project structure created\n117: - [ ] Dependencies installed\n118: - [ ] Development environment ready\n119: \n120: ### Phase 2: Core Implementation\n121: - [ ] [Core feature 1]\n122: - [ ] [Core feature 2]\n123: - [ ] [Core feature 3]\n124: \n125: ### Phase 3: Verification\n126: - [ ] Manual testing complete\n127: - [ ] Edge cases handled\n128: - [ ] Documentation updated\n129: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n134: ## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n135: \n136: | Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n137: |-----------|-------|-------|\n138: | Unit | [Components/functions] | [Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n139: | Integration | [API endpoints/flows] | [Tools] |\n140: | Manual | [User journeys] | Browser |\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: <!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n146: ## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n147: \n148: | Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n149: |------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n150: | [System/Library] | [Internal/External] | [Green/Yellow/Red] | [Impact] |\n151: <!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n152: \n153: ---\n154: \n155: <!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n156: ## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n157: \n158: - **Trigger**: [Conditions requiring rollback]\n159: - **Procedure**: [How to revert changes]\n160: <!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n161: \n162: ---\n163: \n164: <!--\n165: CORE TEMPLATE (~90 lines)\n166: - Essential technical planning\n167: - Simple phase structure\n168: - Add L2/L3 addendums for complexity\n169: -->\n170: \n\n(End of file - total 170 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 1: deep-review\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"implementation\"\n  - \"plan\"\n  - \"name\"\n  - \"template\"\n  - \"plan core\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n_memory:\n  continuity:\n    packet_pointer: \"system-code-graph/036-code-graph-decommission/016-deep-review\"\n    last_updated_at: \"2026-07-28T05:29:53Z\"\n    last_updated_by: \"claude-code\"\n    recent_action: \"Scaffolded the decommission phase child\"\n    next_safe_action: \"Populate requirements from the touchpoint research synthesis\"\n    blockers: []\n    key_files: []","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-code-graph/036-code-graph-decommission/016-deep-review/plan.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Phase 1: deep-review\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"implementation\"\n  - \"plan\"\n  - \"name\"\n  - \"template\"\n  - \"plan core\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n_memory:\n  continuity:\n    packet_pointer: \"system-code-graph/036-code-graph-decommission/016-deep-review\"\n    last_updated_at: \"2026-07-28T05:29:53Z\"\n    last_updated_by: \"claude-code\"\n    recent_action: \"Scaffolded the decommission phase child\"\n    next_safe_action: \"Populate requirements from the touchpoint research synthesis\"\n    blockers: []\n    key_files: []\n    session_dedup:\n      fin