{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785216779426,"sessionID":"ses_058ca7309ffeyGmRDCjINe2gtX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_03_2516uzFlRgK2QzfKoG5f8306","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Canonical review-mode contract for deep-review.\n2: # This file is the single source of truth for review-mode taxonomy,\n3: # convergence settings, cross-reference protocols, downstream render targets,\n4: # and validation expectations.\n5: \n6: meta:\n7:   ownerSkill: deep-review\n8:   reviewModeVersion: 2\n9:   generatedNotice:\n10:     warning: \"Exactly one artifact is machine-generated from this file: render.artifacts[0] (review-contract-snapshot). Its begin/end markers live on that artifact entry, not here. Every other contract-taxonomy consumer is hand-authored; see authoredArtifacts.\"\n11:   sourceOfTruth: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml\n12: \n13: # Core contract definitions consumed by workflows, agents, docs, and validators.\n14: contract:\n15:   defaultTargetType: spec-folder\n16: \n17:   contextSnapshot:\n18:     requiredAtInit: true\n19:     ownerArtifact: deep-review-strategy.md\n20:     section: Known Context\n21:     source: bounded-review-context-snapshot\n22:     bounded: true\n23:     pointerBased: true\n24:     includes:\n25:       - targetPointers\n26:       - behaviorClaims\n27:       - reuseAndConventionPointers\n28:       - riskAreasAndContextGaps\n29:     forbids:\n30:       - deepContextDispatch\n31:       - fullSourceBodyInlining\n32:       - contextLoopReportCreation\n33:       - scopeWideningBeyondReviewTarget\n34: \n35:   # Review target taxonomy.\n36:   targetTypes:\n37:     - id: spec-folder\n38:       cliValue: spec-folder\n39:       label: Spec Folder\n40:       description: Review a single spec folder and its referenced implementation, tests, and release artifacts.\n41:     - id: skill\n42:       cliValue: skill\n43:       label: Skill\n44:       description: Review a skill package including SKILL.md, references, assets, scripts, and runtime integrations.\n45:     - id: agent\n46:       cliValue: agent\n47:       label: Agent\n48:       description: Review a named agent across runtime-specific definitions and capability parity surfaces.\n49:     - id: track\n50:       cliValue: track\n51:       label: Track\n52:       description: Review a spec track spanning multiple child spec folders and shared coordination artifacts.\n53:     - id: files\n54:       cliValue: files\n55:       label: Files\n56:       description: Review an explicit file set plus immediate cross-references required to evaluate shipped behavior.\n57: \n58:   # Simplified review dimensions. Traceability and maintainability absorb the\n59:   # prior seven-dimension model's overlap.\n60:   dimensions:\n61:     - id: correctness\n62:       priority: 1\n63:       label: Correctness\n64:       checks: Validate logic, invariants, state transitions, edge cases, and behavior against observable intent.\n65:       requiredForSeverityCoverage: true\n66:     - id: security\n67:       priority: 2\n68:       label: Security\n69:       checks: Validate trust boundaries, authz/authn behavior, input handling, secrets exposure, and exploit paths.\n70:       requiredForSeverityCoverage: true\n71:     - id: traceability\n72:       priority: 3\n73:       label: Traceability\n74:       checks: Validate spec alignment, completeness, checklist evidence, and cross-reference integrity across linked artifacts.\n75:       requiredForSeverityCoverage: false\n76:     - id: maintainability\n77:       priority: 4\n78:       label: Maintainability\n79:       checks: Validate codebase patterns, documentation quality, clarity, and ease of safe follow-on changes.\n80:       requiredForSeverityCoverage: false\n81: \n82:   # Severity contract stays stable across review outputs.\n83:   severities:\n84:     - id: P0\n85:       weight: 10.0\n86:       label: Blocker\n87:       requiresFileLineEvidence: true\n88:     - id: P1\n89:       weight: 5.0\n90:       label: Required\n91:       requiresFileLineEvidence: true\n92:     - id: P2\n93:       weight: 1.0\n94:       label: Suggestion\n95:       requiresFileLineEvidence: true\n96: \n97:   # Verdicts collapse PASS WITH NOTES into PASS + hasAdvisories metadata.\n98:   verdicts:\n99:     - id: FAIL\n100:       label: Fail\n101:       condition: \"activeP0 > 0 OR any required quality gate fails\"\n102:       nextCommand: /speckit:plan\n103:     - id: CONDITIONAL\n104:       label: Conditional\n105:       condition: \"activeP0 == 0 AND activeP1 > 0\"\n106:       nextCommand: /speckit:plan\n107:     - id: PASS\n108:       label: Pass\n109:       condition: \"activeP0 == 0 AND activeP1 == 0\"\n110:       hasAdvisoriesMetadata: \"Set hasAdvisories=true when activeP2 > 0.\"\n111:       nextCommand: /create:changelog\n112: \n113:   # Binary gates applied after convergence math votes STOP.\n114:   qualityGates:\n115:     - id: evidence\n116:       label: Evidence\n117:       binary: true\n118:       combines:\n119:         - evidence-completeness\n120:         - no-inference-only\n121:       rule: Every active finding must be backed by concrete file:line evidence and may not rely only on inference.\n122:     - id: scope\n123:       label: Scope\n124:       binary: true\n125:       combines:\n126:         - scope-alignment\n127:       rule: Reviewed files, targets, and conclusions must stay inside the declared review scope.\n128:     - id: coverage\n129:       label: Coverage\n130:       binary: true\n131:       combines:\n132:         - severity-coverage\n133:         - cross-reference\n134:       rule: Required dimensions and required traceability protocols must be covered before STOP is allowed.\n135: \n136:   # Review-specific convergence settings calibrated from the v2 research.\n137:   convergence:\n138:     defaults:\n139:       maxIterations: 7\n140:       convergenceThreshold: 0.10\n141:       stuckThreshold: 2\n142:     signals:\n143:       - id: rolling-average\n144:         weight: 0.30\n145:         description: Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings across recent evidence-bearing iterations.\n146:       - id: mad-noise-floor\n147:         weight: 0.25\n148:         description: Robust noise-floor test comparing the latest severity-weighted ratio against MAD-derived churn.\n149:       - id: dimension-coverage\n150:         weight: 0.45\n151:         description: Coverage vote based on required dimension completion plus required protocol coverage stability.\n152:     severityMath:\n153:       refinementMultiplier: 0.5\n154:       p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50\n155:       noFindingsRatio: 0.0\n156:     coverageAge:\n157:       minStabilizationPasses: 1\n158:     thresholds:\n159:       rollingStopThreshold: 0.08\n160:       noProgressThreshold: 0.05\n161:       compositeStopScore: 0.60\n162: \n163:   lifecycleModes:\n164:     - id: new\n165:       description: Create a brand-new review lineage with generation 1 and no parent session.\n166:     - id: resume\n167:       description: Continue the current review lineage without changing generation.\n168:     - id: restart\n169:       description: Start a new generation for the same target and archive the prior review packet state.\n170:     - id: fork\n171:       status: deferred\n172:       description: Reserved compatibility branch. The current runtime does not emit or accept fork review lineages.\n173:     - id: completed-continue\n174:       status: deferred\n175:       description: Reserved compatibility branch. The current runtime does not reopen completed sessions under a completed-continue lineage.\n176: \n177:   lineageFields:\n178:     - sessionId\n179:     - parentSessionId\n180:     - lineageMode\n181:     - generation\n182:     - continuedFromRun\n183: \n184:   reducer:\n185:     enabled: true\n186:     inputs:\n187:       - latestJSONLDelta\n188:       - newIterationFile\n189:       - priorReducedState\n190:     outputs:\n191:       - findingsRegistry\n192:       - dashboardMetrics\n193:       - strategyUpdates\n194:     failureModes:\n195:       malformedDelta: skip-and-warn\n196:       missingIterationFile: no-op-with-error\n197:       schemaMismatch: reject-with-conflict-event\n198:     idempotent: true\n199: \n200:   releaseReadinessStates:\n201:     - id: in-progress\n202:       description: Review is ongoing or coverage is incomplete.\n203:     - id: converged\n204:       description: All dimensions are covered and no new P0/P1 findings appeared in the latest stabilization pass.\n205:     - id: release-blocking\n206:       description: At least one unresolved P0 finding is present.\n207: \n208:   # Cross-reference protocols are typed traceability checks. Core protocols are\n209:   # hard gates; overlay protocols apply only to matching target types.\n210:   crossReferenceProtocols:\n211:     - id: spec_code\n212:       dimension: traceability\n213:       level: core\n214:       appliesTo: [spec-folder, skill, agent, track, files]\n215:       gateClass: hard\n216:       passCriteria: All normative claims resolve to shipped behavior or explicitly documented non-applicability with evidence.\n217:       partialCriteria: Some claims resolve, but one or more claims remain ambiguous or blocked by missing evidence.\n218:       failCriteria: A normative claim contradicts shipped behavior, references missing implementation, or cannot be reconciled.\n219:     - id: checklist_evidence\n220:       dimension: traceability\n221:       level: core\n222:       appliesTo: [spec-folder, skill, agent, track, files]\n223:       gateClass: hard\n224:       passCriteria: Every checked checklist-style claim has supporting evidence and no unsupported completion marks remain.\n225:       partialCriteria: Evidence exists for part of the checked set, but some checked items remain unproven or weakly linked.\n226:       failCriteria: Checked items are unsupported, contradicted by evidence, or materially overstate completion.\n227:     - id: skill_agent\n228:       dimension: traceability\n229:       level: overlay\n230:       appliesTo: [skill]\n231:       gateClass: advisory\n232:       passCriteria: SKILL.md contracts, routing guidance, and referenced runtime agents agree on capabilities and boundaries.\n233:       partialCriteria: Shared intent is consistent, but one or more runtime contracts drift in wording, tools, or expectations.\n234:       failCriteria: SKILL.md and runtime agents materially disagree on capability, routing, permissions, or operating contract.\n235:     - id: agent_cross_runtime\n236:       dimension: traceability\n237:       level: overlay\n238:       appliesTo: [agent]\n239:       gateClass: advisory\n240:       passCriteria: Runtime-specific agent definitions express equivalent behavior, constraints, and evidence requirements.\n241:       partialCriteria: Runtime definitions are broadly aligned but contain non-blocking drift in examples, labels, or metadata.\n242:       failCriteria: Runtime definitions materially diverge in contract, permissions, workflow, or severity/evidence rules.\n243:     - id: feature_catalog_code\n244:       dimension: traceability\n245:       level: overlay\n246:       appliesTo: [skill, spec-folder, track, files]\n247:       gateClass: advisory\n248:       passCriteria: Feature catalog claims match current capability, entry points, and discoverable implementation surfaces.\n249:       partialCriteria: Catalog coverage is incomplete or stale, but no confirmed contradiction to shipped behavior is present.\n250:       failCriteria: Catalog claims are materially false, missing required features, or point to absent implementation.\n251:     - id: playbook_capability\n252:       dimension: traceability\n253:       level: overlay\n254:       appliesTo: [skill, agent, spec-folder]\n255:       gateClass: advisory\n256:       passCriteria: Playbook scenario preconditions, steps, and expected signals are executable against current capability.\n257:       partialCriteria: Scenarios mostly match reality, but one or more steps need updates, clarifications, or narrower scoping.\n258:       failCriteria: Playbook scenarios assume capabilities that do not exist or cannot be executed as documented.\n259: \n260:   # Output contracts consumed by synthesis and replay tooling.\n261:   outputs:\n262:     config:\n263:       pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n264:       machineOwned: false\n265:       fields:\n266:         - sessionId\n267:         - parentSessionId\n268:         - lineageMode\n269:         - generation\n270:         - continuedFromRun\n271:         - releaseReadinessState\n272:     findingsRegistry:\n273:       pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n274:       machineOwned: true\n275:       sections:\n276:         - openFindings\n277:         - resolvedFindings\n278:         - repeatedFindings\n279:         - dimensionCoverage\n280:         - findingsBySeverity\n281:         - convergenceScore\n282:     reviewReport:\n283:       pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n284:       sections:\n285:         - executive-summary\n286:         - planning-trigger\n287:         - active-finding-registry\n288:         - remediation-workstreams\n289:         - spec-seed\n290:         - plan-seed\n291:         - traceability-status\n292:         - deferred-items\n293:         - audit-appendix\n294:     strategy:\n295:       pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n296:       requiredSections:\n297:         - topic\n298:         - review-dimensions\n299:         - completed-dimensions\n300:         - running-findings\n301:         - what-worked\n302:         - what-failed\n303:         - exhausted-approaches\n304:         - ruled-out-directions\n305:         - next-focus\n306:         - known-context\n307:         - cross-reference-status\n308:         - files-under-review\n309:         - review-boundaries\n310:     dashboard:\n311:       pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n312:       machineOwned: true\n313:       sections:\n314:         - status\n315:         - findings-summary\n316:         - dimension-coverage\n317:         - progress\n318:         - next-focus\n319:     pauseSentinel:\n320:       pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n321:       machineOwned: false\n322:       description: Operator-controlled sentinel checked between iterations to pause the loop without discarding state.\n323:     jsonl:\n324:       pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n325:       iterationRecord:\n326:         required:\n327:           - type\n328:           - mode\n329:           - run\n330:           - status\n331:           - focus\n332:           - dimensions\n333:           - filesReviewed\n334:           - findingsCount\n335:           - findingsSummary\n336:           - findingsNew\n337:           - findingDetails\n338:           - newFindingsRatio\n339:           - sessionId\n340:           - generation\n341:           - lineageMode\n342:           - timestamp\n343:           - durationMs\n344:         optional:\n345:           - parentSessionId\n346:           - continuedFromRun\n347:           - findingsRefined\n348:           - findingRefs\n349:           - traceabilityChecks\n350:           - coverage\n351:           - noveltyJustification\n352:           - ruledOut\n353:           - focusTrack\n354:           - scoreEstimate\n355:           - segment\n356:           - convergenceSignals\n357:           - graphEvents\n358:       synthesisEvent:\n359:         required:\n360:           - type\n361:           - event\n362:           - mode\n363:           - totalIterations\n364:           - verdict\n365:           - activeP0\n366:           - activeP1\n367:           - activeP2\n368:           - dimensionCoverage\n369:           - stopReason\n370:           - timestamp\n371: \n372: # Render targets define machine-generated contract fragments. Exactly one\n373: # target is real: the human-readable snapshot rendered by\n374: # render-contract-snapshot.cjs. Everything else that mentions this contract's\n375: # taxonomy (target types, dimensions, severities, verdicts, quality gates,\n376: # convergence, cross-reference protocols) is hand-authored — see\n377: # authoredArtifacts below, not rendered from this file.\n378: render:\n379:   artifacts:\n380:     - id: review-contract-snapshot\n381:       path: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract-snapshot.md\n382:       ownership: generated\n383:       generator: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/render-contract-snapshot.cjs\n384:       format: markdown\n385:       markers:\n386:         begin: \"<!-- BEGIN GENERATED: review-mode-contract/snapshot -->\"\n387:         end: \"<!-- END GENERATED: review-mode-contract/snapshot -->\"\n388:       sections:\n389:         - meta\n390:         - target-types\n391:         - dimensions\n392:         - severities\n393:         - verdicts\n394:         - quality-gates\n395:         - convergence\n396:         - cross-reference-protocols\n397:         - outputs\n398:         - validation\n399: \n400: # Authored artifacts reference this manifest's taxonomy in hand-written prose\n401: # or YAML. They are not machine-rendered and carry no generated markers;\n402: # operators keep them in sync by hand when this contract changes. Each\n403: # entry's enumParityChecked list is mechanically enforced (not aspirational):\n404: # deep-review-contract-parity.vitest.ts confirms every id in those families\n405: # still appears literally in the target file, as a lightweight drift\n406: # tripwire that does not require full rendering.\n407: authoredArtifacts:\n408:   - id: workflow-auto\n409:     path: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\n410:     ownership: authored\n411:     format: yaml\n412:     enumParityChecked:\n413:       - dimensions\n414:       - severities\n415:       - verdicts\n416:       - cross-reference-protocols\n417:     note: Hand-maintained workflow YAML for the :auto command path. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n418:   - id: workflow-confirm\n419:     path: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml\n420:     ownership: authored\n421:     format: yaml\n422:     enumParityChecked:\n423:       - dimensions\n424:       - severities\n425:       - verdicts\n426:       - cross-reference-protocols\n427:     note: Hand-maintained workflow YAML for the :confirm command path. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n428:   - id: agent-opencode\n429:     path: .opencode/agents/deep-review.md\n430:     ownership: authored\n431:     format: markdown\n432:     enumParityChecked:\n433:       - dimensions\n434:       - severities\n435:       - verdicts\n436:     note: Hand-maintained OpenCode agent definition. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n437:   - id: agent-claude\n438:     path: .claude/agents/deep-review.md\n439:     ownership: authored\n440:     format: markdown\n441:     enumParityChecked:\n442:       - dimensions\n443:       - severities\n444:       - verdicts\n445:     note: Hand-maintained Claude Code agent definition. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n446:   - id: quick-reference-review-mode\n447:     path: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md\n448:     ownership: authored\n449:     format: markdown\n450:     enumParityChecked:\n451:       - dimensions\n452:       - severities\n453:       - verdicts\n454:     note: Hand-maintained quick reference. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n455: \n456: # Validator contract for CI, render verification, and drift detection.\n457: validation:\n458:   schemaVersion: 1\n459:   checks:\n460:     - id: schema\n461:       description: Validate this manifest against the canonical review-mode contract schema.\n462:     - id: render-verify\n463:       description: \"Re-render the single review-contract-snapshot artifact (node render-contract-snapshot.cjs --check) and fail on drift. The five authoredArtifacts entries are hand-maintained and are not re-rendered by this check.\"\n464:     - id: marker-integrity\n465:       description: Ensure the review-contract-snapshot artifact contains intact begin/end markers with no overlapping generated blocks.\n466:     - id: enum-parity\n467:       description: \"Confirm the dimension, severity, and verdict ids (plus cross-reference-protocol ids for the two workflow YAMLs) declared in each authoredArtifacts entry's enumParityChecked are still literally present in that file; see deep-review-contract-parity.vitest.ts.\"\n468:     - id: jsonl-parity\n469:       description: Ensure JSONL iteration and synthesis-event fields match the outputs contract.\n470:     - id: lifecycle-parity\n471:       description: \"Ensure lifecycle mode docs and workflow branches agree on the three supported modes: new, resume, and restart.\"\n472:     - id: reducer-contract\n473:       description: Ensure reducer inputs, outputs, and findings-registry metrics are documented consistently across assets and runtime mirrors.\n474:     - id: duplicate-literal-lint\n475:       description: Detect duplicated hard-coded review taxonomy literals outside generated sections.\n476:     - id: runtime-coverage\n477:       description: Ensure every supported runtime deep-review agent has a declared authoredArtifacts entry and parity coverage.\n478:     - id: playbook-assertions\n479:       description: Assert manual testing playbook scenarios reference the canonical simplified contract where applicable.\n\n(End of file - total 479 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Canonical review-mode contract for deep-review.\n# This file is the single source of truth for review-mode taxonomy,\n# convergence settings, cross-reference protocols, downstream render targets,\n# and validation expectations.\n\nmeta:\n  ownerSkill: deep-review\n  reviewModeVersion: 2\n  generatedNotice:\n    warning: \"Exactly one artifact is machine-generated from this file: render.artifacts[0] (review-contract-snapshot). Its begin/end markers live on that artifact entry, not here. Every other contract-taxonomy consumer is hand-authored; see authoredArtifacts.\"\n  sourceOfTruth: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml\n\n# Core contract definitions consumed by workflows, agents, docs, and validators.\ncontract:\n  defaultTargetType: spec-folder\n\n  contextSnapshot:\n    requiredAtInit: true\n    ownerArtifact: deep-review-strategy.md\n    section: Known Context","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml","text":"# Canonical review-mode contract for deep-review.\n# This file is the single source of truth for review-mode taxonomy,\n# convergence settings, cross-reference protocols, downstream render targets,\n# and validation expectations.\n\nmeta:\n  ownerSkill: deep-review\n  reviewModeVersion: 2\n  generatedNotice:\n    warning: \"Exactly one artifact is machine-generated from this file: render.artifacts[0] (review-contract-snapshot). Its begin/end markers live on that artifact entry, not here. Every other contract-taxonomy consumer is hand-authored; see authoredArtifacts.\"\n  sourceOfTruth: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml\n\n# Core contract definitions consumed by workflows, agents, docs, and validators.\ncontract:\n  defaultTargetType: spec-folder\n\n  contextSnapshot:\n    requiredAtInit: true\n    ownerArtifact: deep-review-strategy.md\n    section: Known Context\n    source: bounded-review-context-snapshot\n    bounded: true\n    pointerBased: true\n    includes:\n      - targetPointers\n      - behaviorClaims\n      - reuseAndConventionPointers\n      - riskAreasAndContextGaps\n    forbids:\n      - deepContextDispatch\n      - fullSourceBodyInlining\n      - contextLoopReportCreation\n      - scopeWideningBeyondReviewTarget\n\n  # Review target taxonomy.\n  targetTypes:\n    - id: spec-folder\n      cliValue: spec-folder\n      label: Spec Folder\n      description: Review a single spec folder and its referenced implementation, tests, and release artifacts.\n    - id: skill\n      cliValue: skill\n      label: Skill\n      description: Review a skill package including SKILL.md, references, assets, scripts, and runtime integrations.\n    - id: agent\n      cliValue: agent\n      label: Agent\n      description: Review a named agent across runtime-specific definitions and capability parity surfaces.\n    - id: track\n      cliValue: track\n      label: Track\n      description: Review a spec track spanning multiple child spec folders and shared coordination artifacts.\n    - id: files\n      cliValue: files\n      label: Files\n      description: Review an explicit file set plus immediate cross-references required to evaluate shipped behavior.\n\n  # Simplified review dimensions. Traceability and maintainability absorb the\n  # prior seven-dimension model's overlap.\n  dimensions:\n    - id: correctness\n      priority: 1\n      label: Correctness\n      checks: Validate logic, invariants, state transitions, edge cases, and behavior against observable intent.\n      requiredForSeverityCoverage: true\n    - id: security\n      priority: 2\n      label: Security\n      checks: Validate trust boundaries, authz/authn behavior, input handling, secrets exposure, and exploit paths.\n      requiredForSeverityCoverage: true\n    - id: traceability\n      priority: 3\n      label: Traceability\n      checks: Validate spec alignment, completeness, checklist evidence, and cross-reference integrity across linked artifacts.\n      requiredForSeverityCoverage: false\n    - id: maintainability\n      priority: 4\n      label: Maintainability\n      checks: Validate codebase patterns, documentation quality, clarity, and ease of safe follow-on changes.\n      requiredForSeverityCoverage: false\n\n  # Severity contract stays stable across review outputs.\n  severities:\n    - id: P0\n      weight: 10.0\n      label: Blocker\n      requiresFileLineEvidence: true\n    - id: P1\n      weight: 5.0\n      label: Required\n      requiresFileLineEvidence: true\n    - id: P2\n      weight: 1.0\n      label: Suggestion\n      requiresFileLineEvidence: true\n\n  # Verdicts collapse PASS WITH NOTES into PASS + hasAdvisories metadata.\n  verdicts:\n    - id: FAIL\n      label: Fail\n      condition: \"activeP0 > 0 OR any required quality gate fails\"\n      nextCommand: /speckit:plan\n    - id: CONDITIONAL\n      label: Conditional\n      condition: \"activeP0 == 0 AND activeP1 > 0\"\n      nextCommand: /speckit:plan\n    - id: PASS\n      label: Pass\n      condition: \"activeP0 == 0 AND activeP1 == 0\"\n      hasAdvisoriesMetadata: \"Set hasAdvisories=true when activeP2 > 0.\"\n      nextCommand: /create:changelog\n\n  # Binary gates applied after convergence math votes STOP.\n  qualityGates:\n    - id: evidence\n      label: Evidence\n      binary: true\n      combines:\n        - evidence-completeness\n        - no-inference-only\n      rule: Every active finding must be backed by concrete file:line evidence and may not rely only on inference.\n    - id: scope\n      label: Scope\n      binary: true\n      combines:\n        - scope-alignment\n      rule: Reviewed files, targets, and conclusions must stay inside the declared review scope.\n    - id: coverage\n      label: Coverage\n      binary: true\n      combines:\n        - severity-coverage\n        - cross-reference\n      rule: Required dimensions and required traceability protocols must be covered before STOP is allowed.\n\n  # Review-specific convergence settings calibrated from the v2 research.\n  convergence:\n    defaults:\n      maxIterations: 7\n      convergenceThreshold: 0.10\n      stuckThreshold: 2\n    signals:\n      - id: rolling-average\n        weight: 0.30\n        description: Rolling average of severity-weighted new findings across recent evidence-bearing iterations.\n      - id: mad-noise-floor\n        weight: 0.25\n        description: Robust noise-floor test comparing the latest severity-weighted ratio against MAD-derived churn.\n      - id: dimension-coverage\n        weight: 0.45\n        description: Coverage vote based on required dimension completion plus required protocol coverage stability.\n    severityMath:\n      refinementMultiplier: 0.5\n      p0OverrideMinRatio: 0.50\n      noFindingsRatio: 0.0\n    coverageAge:\n      minStabilizationPasses: 1\n    thresholds:\n      rollingStopThreshold: 0.08\n      noProgressThreshold: 0.05\n      compositeStopScore: 0.60\n\n  lifecycleModes:\n    - id: new\n      description: Create a brand-new review lineage with generation 1 and no parent session.\n    - id: resume\n      description: Continue the current review lineage without changing generation.\n    - id: restart\n      description: Start a new generation for the same target and archive the prior review packet state.\n    - id: fork\n      status: deferred\n      description: Reserved compatibility branch. The current runtime does not emit or accept fork review lineages.\n    - id: completed-continue\n      status: deferred\n      description: Reserved compatibility branch. The current runtime does not reopen completed sessions under a completed-continue lineage.\n\n  lineageFields:\n    - sessionId\n    - parentSessionId\n    - lineageMode\n    - generation\n    - continuedFromRun\n\n  reducer:\n    enabled: true\n    inputs:\n      - latestJSONLDelta\n      - newIterationFile\n      - priorReducedState\n    outputs:\n      - findingsRegistry\n      - dashboardMetrics\n      - strategyUpdates\n    failureModes:\n      malformedDelta: skip-and-warn\n      missingIterationFile: no-op-with-error\n      schemaMismatch: reject-with-conflict-event\n    idempotent: true\n\n  releaseReadinessStates:\n    - id: in-progress\n      description: Review is ongoing or coverage is incomplete.\n    - id: converged\n      description: All dimensions are covered and no new P0/P1 findings appeared in the latest stabilization pass.\n    - id: release-blocking\n      description: At least one unresolved P0 finding is present.\n\n  # Cross-reference protocols are typed traceability checks. Core protocols are\n  # hard gates; overlay protocols apply only to matching target types.\n  crossReferenceProtocols:\n    - id: spec_code\n      dimension: traceability\n      level: core\n      appliesTo: [spec-folder, skill, agent, track, files]\n      gateClass: hard\n      passCriteria: All normative claims resolve to shipped behavior or explicitly documented non-applicability with evidence.\n      partialCriteria: Some claims resolve, but one or more claims remain ambiguous or blocked by missing evidence.\n      failCriteria: A normative claim contradicts shipped behavior, references missing implementation, or cannot be reconciled.\n    - id: checklist_evidence\n      dimension: traceability\n      level: core\n      appliesTo: [spec-folder, skill, agent, track, files]\n      gateClass: hard\n      passCriteria: Every checked checklist-style claim has supporting evidence and no unsupported completion marks remain.\n      partialCriteria: Evidence exists for part of the checked set, but some checked items remain unproven or weakly linked.\n      failCriteria: Checked items are unsupported, contradicted by evidence, or materially overstate completion.\n    - id: skill_agent\n      dimension: traceability\n      level: overlay\n      appliesTo: [skill]\n      gateClass: advisory\n      passCriteria: SKILL.md contracts, routing guidance, and referenced runtime agents agree on capabilities and boundaries.\n      partialCriteria: Shared intent is consistent, but one or more runtime contracts drift in wording, tools, or expectations.\n      failCriteria: SKILL.md and runtime agents materially disagree on capability, routing, permissions, or operating contract.\n    - id: agent_cross_runtime\n      dimension: traceability\n      level: overlay\n      appliesTo: [agent]\n      gateClass: advisory\n      passCriteria: Runtime-specific agent definitions express equivalent behavior, constraints, and evidence requirements.\n      partialCriteria: Runtime definitions are broadly aligned but contain non-blocking drift in examples, labels, or metadata.\n      failCriteria: Runtime definitions materially diverge in contract, permissions, workflow, or severity/evidence rules.\n    - id: feature_catalog_code\n      dimension: traceability\n      level: overlay\n      appliesTo: [skill, spec-folder, track, files]\n      gateClass: advisory\n      passCriteria: Feature catalog claims match current capability, entry points, and discoverable implementation surfaces.\n      partialCriteria: Catalog coverage is incomplete or stale, but no confirmed contradiction to shipped behavior is present.\n      failCriteria: Catalog claims are materially false, missing required features, or point to absent implementation.\n    - id: playbook_capability\n      dimension: traceability\n      level: overlay\n      appliesTo: [skill, agent, spec-folder]\n      gateClass: advisory\n      passCriteria: Playbook scenario preconditions, steps, and expected signals are executable against current capability.\n      partialCriteria: Scenarios mostly match reality, but one or more steps need updates, clarifications, or narrower scoping.\n      failCriteria: Playbook scenarios assume capabilities that do not exist or cannot be executed as documented.\n\n  # Output contracts consumed by synthesis and replay tooling.\n  outputs:\n    config:\n      pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n      machineOwned: false\n      fields:\n        - sessionId\n        - parentSessionId\n        - lineageMode\n        - generation\n        - continuedFromRun\n        - releaseReadinessState\n    findingsRegistry:\n      pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n      machineOwned: true\n      sections:\n        - openFindings\n        - resolvedFindings\n        - repeatedFindings\n        - dimensionCoverage\n        - findingsBySeverity\n        - convergenceScore\n    reviewReport:\n      pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n      sections:\n        - executive-summary\n        - planning-trigger\n        - active-finding-registry\n        - remediation-workstreams\n        - spec-seed\n        - plan-seed\n        - traceability-status\n        - deferred-items\n        - audit-appendix\n    strategy:\n      pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n      requiredSections:\n        - topic\n        - review-dimensions\n        - completed-dimensions\n        - running-findings\n        - what-worked\n        - what-failed\n        - exhausted-approaches\n        - ruled-out-directions\n        - next-focus\n        - known-context\n        - cross-reference-status\n        - files-under-review\n        - review-boundaries\n    dashboard:\n      pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n      machineOwned: true\n      sections:\n        - status\n        - findings-summary\n        - dimension-coverage\n        - progress\n        - next-focus\n    pauseSentinel:\n      pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n      machineOwned: false\n      description: Operator-controlled sentinel checked between iterations to pause the loop without discarding state.\n    jsonl:\n      pathPattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n      iterationRecord:\n        required:\n          - type\n          - mode\n          - run\n          - status\n          - focus\n          - dimensions\n          - filesReviewed\n          - findingsCount\n          - findingsSummary\n          - findingsNew\n          - findingDetails\n          - newFindingsRatio\n          - sessionId\n          - generation\n          - lineageMode\n          - timestamp\n          - durationMs\n        optional:\n          - parentSessionId\n          - continuedFromRun\n          - findingsRefined\n          - findingRefs\n          - traceabilityChecks\n          - coverage\n          - noveltyJustification\n          - ruledOut\n          - focusTrack\n          - scoreEstimate\n          - segment\n          - convergenceSignals\n          - graphEvents\n      synthesisEvent:\n        required:\n          - type\n          - event\n          - mode\n          - totalIterations\n          - verdict\n          - activeP0\n          - activeP1\n          - activeP2\n          - dimensionCoverage\n          - stopReason\n          - timestamp\n\n# Render targets define machine-generated contract fragments. Exactly one\n# target is real: the human-readable snapshot rendered by\n# render-contract-snapshot.cjs. Everything else that mentions this contract's\n# taxonomy (target types, dimensions, severities, verdicts, quality gates,\n# convergence, cross-reference protocols) is hand-authored — see\n# authoredArtifacts below, not rendered from this file.\nrender:\n  artifacts:\n    - id: review-contract-snapshot\n      path: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract-snapshot.md\n      ownership: generated\n      generator: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/scripts/render-contract-snapshot.cjs\n      format: markdown\n      markers:\n        begin: \"<!-- BEGIN GENERATED: review-mode-contract/snapshot -->\"\n        end: \"<!-- END GENERATED: review-mode-contract/snapshot -->\"\n      sections:\n        - meta\n        - target-types\n        - dimensions\n        - severities\n        - verdicts\n        - quality-gates\n        - convergence\n        - cross-reference-protocols\n        - outputs\n        - validation\n\n# Authored artifacts reference this manifest's taxonomy in hand-written prose\n# or YAML. They are not machine-rendered and carry no generated markers;\n# operators keep them in sync by hand when this contract changes. Each\n# entry's enumParityChecked list is mechanically enforced (not aspirational):\n# deep-review-contract-parity.vitest.ts confirms every id in those families\n# still appears literally in the target file, as a lightweight drift\n# tripwire that does not require full rendering.\nauthoredArtifacts:\n  - id: workflow-auto\n    path: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\n    ownership: authored\n    format: yaml\n    enumParityChecked:\n      - dimensions\n      - severities\n      - verdicts\n      - cross-reference-protocols\n    note: Hand-maintained workflow YAML for the :auto command path. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n  - id: workflow-confirm\n    path: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-confirm.yaml\n    ownership: authored\n    format: yaml\n    enumParityChecked:\n      - dimensions\n      - severities\n      - verdicts\n      - cross-reference-protocols\n    note: Hand-maintained workflow YAML for the :confirm command path. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n  - id: agent-opencode\n    path: .opencode/agents/deep-review.md\n    ownership: authored\n    format: markdown\n    enumParityChecked:\n      - dimensions\n      - severities\n      - verdicts\n    note: Hand-maintained OpenCode agent definition. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n  - id: agent-claude\n    path: .claude/agents/deep-review.md\n    ownership: authored\n    format: markdown\n    enumParityChecked:\n      - dimensions\n      - severities\n      - verdicts\n    note: Hand-maintained Claude Code agent definition. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n  - id: quick-reference-review-mode\n    path: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/quick-reference.md\n    ownership: authored\n    format: markdown\n    enumParityChecked:\n      - dimensions\n      - severities\n      - verdicts\n    note: Hand-maintained quick reference. References this contract's taxonomy in prose; not machine-rendered from this manifest.\n\n# Validator contract for CI, render verification, and drift detection.\nvalidation:\n  schemaVersion: 1\n  checks:\n    - id: schema\n      description: Validate this manifest against the canonical review-mode contract schema.\n    - id: render-verify\n      description: \"Re-render the single review-contract-snapshot artifact (node render-contract-snapshot.cjs --check) and fail on drift. The five authoredArtifacts entries are hand-maintained and are not re-rendered by this check.\"\n    - id: marker-integrity\n      description: Ensure the review-contract-snapshot artifact contains intact begin/end markers with no overlapping generated blocks.\n    - id: enum-parity\n      description: \"Confirm the dimension, severity, and verdict ids (plus cross-reference-protocol ids for the two workflow YAMLs) declared in each authoredArtifacts entry's enumParityChecked are still literally present in that file; see deep-review-contract-parity.vitest.ts.\"\n    - id: jsonl-parity\n      description: Ensure JSONL iteration and synthesis-event fields match the outputs contract.\n    - id: lifecycle-parity\n      description: \"Ensure lifecycle mode docs and workflow branches agree on the three supported modes: new, resume, and restart.\"\n    - id: reducer-contract\n      description: Ensure reducer inputs, outputs, and findings-registry metrics are documented consistently across assets and runtime mirrors.\n    - id: duplicate-literal-lint\n      description: Detect duplicated hard-coded review taxonomy literals outside generated sections.\n    - id: runtime-coverage\n      description: Ensure every supported runtime deep-review agent has a declared authoredArtifacts entry and parity coverage.\n    - id: playbook-assertions\n      description: Assert manual testing playbook scenarios reference the canonical simplified contract where applicable.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":479,"totalLines":479,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/review-mode-contract.yaml","time":{"start":1785216779419,"end":1785216779424}},"id":"prt_fa73643530011CsGKVQQzeeV6G","sessionID":"ses_058ca7309ffeyGmRDCjINe2gtX","messageID":"msg_fa7362271001f7FyaJ8CMmhS2R"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785216779853,"sessionID":"ses_058ca7309ffeyGmRDCjINe2gtX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_04_wpt39n2HhJfOAXvb7jZO9089","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Deep Review Convergence Signals\"\n3: description: \"Focused reference for severity-weighted stop signals, P0 overrides, quality gates, and graph-aware blocked-stop checks.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review convergence signals\"\n6:   - \"review stop signals\"\n7:   - \"severity weighted convergence\"\n8:   - \"review blocked stop\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: implementation\n11: version: 1.11.0.3\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Convergence Signals\n15: \n16: This reference names the live stop signals. Use `references/convergence/convergence.md` as the hub when you need algorithms, examples, and sibling threshold notes.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: Deep-review convergence is a release-readiness decision. The loop stops only when severity-weighted findings stabilize, dimension coverage is complete, quality gates pass, and no P0 override is active.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. SIGNALS\n27: \n28: | Signal | Meaning | Blocks STOP When |\n29: |--------|---------|------------------|\n30: | Severity-weighted new findings | Weighted P0/P1/P2 discovery ratio for the latest iteration | Above the configured threshold |\n31: | Rolling stop average | Stabilized trend across recent iterations | Still above the stop band |\n32: | Dimension coverage | Required review dimensions and traceability overlays covered | Any required dimension is missing |\n33: | Quality-gate bundle | Evidence, scope, coverage, P0, density, hotspot, claim, candidate, graphless gates | Any required gate fails |\n34: | Graph-aware blind spot check | Coverage graph sees unresolved structural gaps | Graph blockers remain active |\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 3. P0 OVERRIDE\n39: \n40: Any new P0 forces at least one more iteration. The override exists because a new blocker changes the release verdict, even if the rest of the stop math appears stable.\n41: \n42: P0 handling requires:\n43: \n44: - File and line evidence.\n45: - Adversarial self-check.\n46: - Active registry update.\n47: - Replay in synthesis before PASS is legal.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 4. LEGAL STOP\n52: \n53: STOP is legal only when all of these are true:\n54: \n55: 1. New findings are below threshold.\n56: 2. Rolling trend is stable.\n57: 3. All required dimensions are covered.\n58: 4. The quality-gate bundle passes.\n59: 5. No unresolved P0 remains.\n60: 6. Graph-aware blockers are absent or explicitly unavailable with fallback evidence.\n61: \n62: If any item fails, the workflow emits `blocked_stop` and continues or routes to recovery.\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: ## 5. SIBLING CONTRAST\n67: \n68: Do not carry thresholds across deep skills:\n69: \n70: | Skill | Primary Signal | Default Threshold |\n71: |-------|----------------|-------------------|\n72: | `deep-review` | Severity-weighted P0/P1/P2 new findings | `0.10` |\n73: | `deep-research` | Novelty/newInfoRatio over research knowledge | `0.05` |\n74: | `deep-ai-council` | Planning agreement with critique blocker check | Council-specific, not interchangeable |\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: ## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n79: \n80: - `references/convergence/convergence.md` for the full stop contract.\n81: - `references/state/state-outputs.md` for dashboard and report fields that display convergence.\n82: - `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md` for reducer-owned gate state.\n\n(End of file - total 82 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review Convergence Signals\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for severity-weighted stop signals, P0 overrides, quality gates, and graph-aware blocked-stop checks.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review convergence signals\"\n  - \"review stop signals\"\n  - \"severity weighted convergence\"\n  - \"review blocked stop\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review Convergence Signals\n\nThis reference names the live stop signals. Use `references/convergence/convergence.md` as the hub when you need algorithms, examples, and sibling threshold notes.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Deep Review Convergence Signals\"\ndescription: \"Focused reference for severity-weighted stop signals, P0 overrides, quality gates, and graph-aware blocked-stop checks.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"deep review convergence signals\"\n  - \"review stop signals\"\n  - \"severity weighted convergence\"\n  - \"review blocked stop\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.11.0.3\n---\n\n# Deep Review Convergence Signals\n\nThis reference names the live stop signals. Use `references/convergence/convergence.md` as the hub when you need algorithms, examples, and sibling threshold notes.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDeep-review convergence is a release-readiness decision. The loop stops only when severity-weighted findings stabilize, dimension coverage is complete, quality gates pass, and no P0 override is active.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SIGNALS\n\n| Signal | Meaning | Blocks STOP When |\n|--------|---------|------------------|\n| Severity-weighted new findings | Weighted P0/P1/P2 discovery ratio for the latest iteration | Above the configured threshold |\n| Rolling stop average | Stabilized trend across recent iterations | Still above the stop band |\n| Dimension coverage | Required review dimensions and traceability overlays covered | Any required dimension is missing |\n| Quality-gate bundle | Evidence, scope, coverage, P0, density, hotspot, claim, candidate, graphless gates | Any required gate fails |\n| Graph-aware blind spot check | Coverage graph sees unresolved structural gaps | Graph blockers remain active |\n\n---\n\n## 3. P0 OVERRIDE\n\nAny new P0 forces at least one more iteration. The override exists because a new blocker changes the release verdict, even if the rest of the stop math appears stable.\n\nP0 handling requires:\n\n- File and line evidence.\n- Adversarial self-check.\n- Active registry update.\n- Replay in synthesis before PASS is legal.\n\n---\n\n## 4. LEGAL STOP\n\nSTOP is legal only when all of these are true:\n\n1. New findings are below threshold.\n2. Rolling trend is stable.\n3. All required dimensions are covered.\n4. The quality-gate bundle passes.\n5. No unresolved P0 remains.\n6. Graph-aware blockers are absent or explicitly unavailable with fallback evidence.\n\nIf any item fails, the workflow emits `blocked_stop` and continues or routes to recovery.\n\n---\n\n## 5. SIBLING CONTRAST\n\nDo not carry thresholds across deep skills:\n\n| Skill | Primary Signal | Default Threshold |\n|-------|----------------|-------------------|\n| `deep-review` | Severity-weighted P0/P1/P2 new findings | `0.10` |\n| `deep-research` | Novelty/newInfoRatio over research knowledge | `0.05` |\n| `deep-ai-council` | Planning agreement with critique blocker check | Council-specific, not interchangeable |\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED RESOURCES\n\n- `references/convergence/convergence.md` for the full stop contract.\n- `references/state/state-outputs.md` for dashboard and report fields that display convergence.\n- `references/state/state-reducer-registry.md` for reducer-owned gate state.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":82,"totalLines":82,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence-signals.md","time":{"start":1785216779845,"end":1785216779851}},"id":"prt_fa73644fe001zSRlGuQqyIG2nh","sessionID":"ses_058ca7309ffeyGmRDCjINe2gtX","messageID":"msg_fa7362271001f7FyaJ8CMmhS2R"}}
